Z||000000||frontal lobe||08-26-2000||12:21 AM||||I want to buy an engine from Ron Smigla Jr.  However, he's in the Pittsburg area and I'm in Milwaukee.  I don't feel like hiking out there (at least 10 hours drive) and back to pick it up.  Does anyone have experience shipping engines?  Who did you use?  Estimated price to get it to Milwaukee?<P>Thanks in advance.  I'm hot to get the engine so I can get the '86GT on the road again.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||08-26-2000||12:42 AM||||Consider air freight. It must be on a pallet or stand. All fluids drained.<P>I air freighted an engine from Canada to the US for $325. <P>For that distance it would be substantially cheaper and fast.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||08-26-2000||12:42 AM||||Consider air freight. It must be on a pallet or stand. All fluids drained.<P>I air freighted an engine from Canada to the US for $325. <P>For that distance it would be substantially cheaper and fast.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-26-2000||02:34 PM||||Look in the phonebook for trucking companies. should be cheaper than air.<P>Either way it will need palletized or better yet crated on a pallet. It has to be attached to the pallet so it can't move or flip. It has to be purged of all fluids.<P>unless you have loading docks and/or forklifts on each end you should make sure you specify it be picked up and delivered in trucks with lift gates on back.||||reg||1
